.rm 65
.bd
NAME
.in +5
.br
.bd
setdev
- show or set a Micronix kernel's root and swap devices, and stamp the
root device's driver into it
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
SYNTAX
.in +5
.br
.bd
setdev kernel [ root swap ]
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
DESCRIPTION
.in +5
.br
Setdev reads the symbol table of a Micronix kernel and prints or
changes the _rootdev and _swapdev words in it.  With no devices it
prints them; with two it writes them.
.sp
A device is written either as major/minor - 3/0 - or as a plain
number, decimal or 0x hex, so 3/0, 0x300 and 768 all agree.
.sp
It also prints the appended driver modules the kernel carries and what
its slot holds.  Setting the devices stamps one of those modules into
the slot as well: the kernel is linked with no disk drivers and a
page-sized hole in its text, and the driver it needs to mount root is
chosen here, at install time.  The driver is not named - it is the
module whose header says it serves the major that root names - so the
stamp and root are written in one pass and cannot disagree.
.sp
This replaces the old ddt recipe, which searched the kernel for the
bytes of the root device it expected to find.  The kernel carries a
symbol table, so _rootdev and _swapdev say where they are, and nothing
has to be guessed.
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
SEE ALSO
.in +5
